[
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // Offline panels (cannot be opened by capture.py): battle GameOverPanel
  // (win / dead), story-mode GameOver desc, EndGamePanel + SaveLegendPanel,
  // battle PausePanel, skill cut-ins. Written from inventory/*.txt + decompiled
  // code only - every rule here is either (a) an unambiguous vertical /
  // rotated box, or (b) shrink-only (bestFit inside the existing box), so it
  // cannot overlap neighbours even if the live layout differs from the
  // serialized one. Nothing here changes strings.
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

  // ---- battle GameOverPanel: Dead ("You are dead") ---------------------------
  {
    "id": "go-dead-vertical-fallback",
    "comment": "Dead/Container has a Vertical and a Horizontal copy of the two death lines, toggled by LocalizationDisplayPanel on SystemSettings.IsChineseLanguage. With the plugin's ForceHorizontalLanguageBranches the Horizontal copy (1192x66 / 971x94 at 40px) is active and needs nothing. The Vertical copy is a 56px-wide one-glyph-per-line column (56x297 / 56x882); if a user turns the language patch off, English would stack letter by letter. Mirror the Horizontal geometry onto it so it reads as normal lines in that case (no-op while inactive).",
    "path": "**/GameOverPanel/Dead/Container/Vertical/Text (1)",
    "rect": { "anchoredPos": [250, -129], "sizeDelta": [1192, 66] },
    "text": { "hOverflow": "Wrap", "vOverflow": "Truncate", "alignment": "UpperLeft" }
  },
  {
    "id": "go-dead-vertical-fallback-2",
    "comment": "Second line of the Vertical fallback, see go-dead-vertical-fallback.",
    "path": "**/GameOverPanel/Dead/Container/Vertical/Text (2)",
    "rect": { "anchoredPos": [250, -192], "sizeDelta": [971, 94] },
    "text": { "hOverflow": "Wrap", "vOverflow": "Truncate", "alignment": "UpperLeft" }
  },
  {
   "id": "go-dead-buttons",
   "comment": "Restart / Main Menu buttons on the battle dead screen: 300x70 LowerCenter labels at 40px. They are LeanLocalizedText labels (System/Restart, System/GoMenu), so the resolver - and the patch's own 'Go back to the main menu' - never reaches them. With LOM_Strings_EN they read 'Restart' (148px) and 'Main Menu' (231px) and fit at 40; with the strings plugin off XUnity gives 'New Game' (217px) and 'Return to Main Menu' (435px), which would wrap and lose its second line. The buttons have no background sprite, so shrink rather than widen: bestFit 22..40 is a no-op for the short labels and puts the long one on one line at 27px.",
   "paths": [
    "**/GameOverPanel/Dead/Container/MenuButton_*/*/Text"
   ],
   "text": {
    "bestFit": true,
    "minSize": 22,
    "maxSize": 40,
    "hOverflow": "Wrap",
    "vOverflow": "Truncate"
   },
   "onTextChange": true
  },

  // ---- battle GameOverPanel: WinPanel (big 勝 / 敗 stamp) ----------------------
  {
   "id": "go-win-stamp",
   "comment": "VictoryText / DefeatText are TextMeshPro 800x800 boxes at fontSize 550 (Center/Middle) holding one calligraphic glyph (勝 / 敗) in DFT_S5_SDF_Battle_001/002 (39 / 45 glyphs, no Latin, no per-asset fallbacks). They are LeanLocalizedTextMeshProUGUI labels (System/BattleVictory / System/BattleLose), which bypass the resolver, so the patch's 'Victory' / 'Defeat' never reach them: XUnity gives 'Win' / 'Defeated', drawn from the plugin's global Source Han Serif TMP fallback - 1169px / 2500px at 550, over the whole result column. autoSize 100..550 with wordWrap off is a no-op for the untouched glyph and shrinks the word to the box: 'Win' ~348px, 'Defeated' ~163px. Width 800->740 so the word ends at x=1158, left of the HeaderText/ResultItem column at x=1185. No font swap (it would break the glyph when the text is not translated).",
   "paths": [
    "**/GameOverPanel/WinPanel/VictoryText",
    "**/GameOverPanel/WinPanel/DefeatText"
   ],
   "rect": {
    "dw": -60
   },
   "tmp": {
    "autoSize": true,
    "minSize": 100,
    "maxSize": 550,
    "wordWrap": false,
    "alignment": "Center",
    "overflow": "Overflow"
   },
   "onTextChange": true
  },

  // ---- story-mode GameOver (GameOverController) -------------------------------
  {
   "id": "go-story-desc-horizontal",
   "comment": "Story game over description. The previous path (**/HorizontalDesc/GameOverDescText(Clone)) never matched: in level4 the non-Chinese container is /Canvas/Horizontal/DescText (1370x266, VerticalLayoutGroup with childControlWidth/Height), so the GameOverDescText clone already gets min(preferred, 1370) wide and needs no width. What is left is the prefab's lineSpacing 0.8: at 35px English lines are 40.3px apart for 40px of Latin ink (ascender top to descender bottom), so descenders touch the next line's ascenders. 1.0 gives 50.4px; the longest death text (5 lines at 1370) is 252px, inside the 266px container.",
   "path": "/Canvas/Horizontal/DescText/GameOverDescText(Clone)",
   "text": {
    "lineSpacing": 1.0
   }
  },

  // ---- EndGamePanel (ending book) + SaveLegendPanel ---------------------------
  // The SaveLegendPanel Empty/Text spines, Detail/Name, ConfirmPanel Message and buttons are covered by
  // the ** rules in 41_library.json (lib-legend-*).
  {
   "id": "endgame-desc-fit",
   "comment": "Ending description (EndGamePanel/Desc, 25px UpperLeft, Wrap, vOverflow Overflow, no best fit, with a TextSizePanel that only reacts in OnEnable). English endings run to ~411 characters and overflowed the page. Give the box 300px and best fit 18-28 with Truncate, so short endings stay large and the longest one shrinks to fit. onTextChange because EndGamePanel.Open sets the text on a panel that is already active. Both copies (Library on the title screen, the end-of-game panel) are matched.",
   "paths": ["**/EndGamePanel/Desc"],
   "onTextChange": true,
   "rect": { "height": 300 },
   "text": { "bestFit": true, "minSize": 18, "maxSize": 28, "hOverflow": "Wrap", "vOverflow": "Truncate" }
  },
  {
   "id": "endgame-savelegend-title",
   "comment": "SaveLegendPanel heading (System/SaveLegnedText, 789x103 UpperCenter box, 50px; both copies: story TopPanel and the title-library EndGamePanel). The text is now 'Recording Your Legend of Mortal Story' (LOM_Strings_EN), 1001px at 50, which wraps and loses its second line to the 103px box. bestFit 32..50 settles on one line at 39px (781px): two lines need 2 x 1.44 x size <= 103, i.e. 35px or less, so the one-line fit at 39 wins.",
   "paths": [
    "**/EndGamePanel/SaveLegendPanel/Title"
   ],
   "text": {
    "bestFit": true,
    "minSize": 32,
    "maxSize": 50,
    "hOverflow": "Wrap",
    "vOverflow": "Truncate",
    "alignment": "UpperCenter"
   },
   "onTextChange": true
  },
  {
    "id": "endgame-close-tmp-label",
    "comment": "SaveLegendPanel/CloseButton_02 carries the same 9x50 vertical TMP label ('Leave', one glyph per line) as the library close buttons (41_library lib-close-tmp-label covers only **/LibraryPanel/**). It is normally inactive; if the game turns it on, make it a horizontal 90x26 line centred under the 90x90 button.",
    "paths": ["**/EndGamePanel/**/CloseButton_02/*/Text (TMP)"],
    "rect": { "x": 0, "y": -92, "width": 90, "height": 26 },
    "tmp": { "wordWrap": false, "alignment": "Center", "overflow": "Overflow", "fontSize": 20 }
  },

  // ---- battle skill cut-ins (Friend/EnemySkillCutPanel) ------------------------
  {
   "id": "skillcut-title",
   "comment": "Skill name on the tilted friend/enemy cut-in banner (rot +10 / -10, 500x100 box, 60px DFXingShu -> Palatino 54, hOverflow Overflow in the prefab). BattleSkillCutPanel shows BattleSkill/Name/<key> (resolver) only for skills with _enableCutInUI (girl9, player_1, player_shield_1, player_block, brother2, brother4, sister1_1, special3, girl4 - not brother1). The longest, 'Breakthrough of Cloud Pass · Thunder Shakes the Nine Heavens' (special3), is 1547px at 54 and ran far past the 580px banner art. Keep the tilt (it is the banner's design) and let the name wrap inside the box with bestFit 26..54: special3 two lines at 32px, 'Heaven and Earth Silent Power' (sister1_1) two lines at ~48px, the other seven one line at 54. Alignment stays UpperLeft / UpperRight from the prefab.",
   "paths": [
    "**/FriendSkillCutPanel*/Title",
    "**/EnemySkillCutPanel*/Title"
   ],
   "text": {
    "bestFit": true,
    "minSize": 26,
    "maxSize": 54,
    "hOverflow": "Wrap",
    "vOverflow": "Truncate"
   },
   "onTextChange": true
  },

  // ---- battle PausePanel ------------------------------------------------------
  // LoadGamePanel / SystemSettingPanel copies inside PausePanel are covered by the ** rules in
  // 40_settings.json / 42_loadgame.json. KeyboardSetting/Container rows share the prefab with
  // Level_3/ReadyPanel (battle HUD area) and are not touched here.
  {
   "id": "pause-border-buttons",
   "comment": "Battle pause menu strip (Border/MenuButton_Continue/Load/Keyboard/Setting/Title/Giveup): 300x50 MiddleCenter labels at 30px. They are LeanLocalizedText labels (System/Menu/*), so the patch's resolver strings (e.g. 'Read the game instructions', 422px) never reach them. With LOM_Strings_EN every label fits at 30 (widest 'Keyboard Settings', 280px; 'Surrender' via XUnity), and so do XUnity's own labels with the strings plugin off (widest also 'Keyboard Settings'). Kept as a safety net: bestFit 20..30 only shrinks a label that would otherwise wrap.",
   "paths": [
    "**/PausePanel/Border/MenuButton_*/*/Text"
   ],
   "text": {
    "bestFit": true,
    "minSize": 20,
    "maxSize": 30,
    "hOverflow": "Wrap",
    "vOverflow": "Truncate",
    "alignment": "MiddleCenter"
   },
   "onTextChange": true
  },
  {
   "id": "pause-info-header",
