  {
   "id": "skillcut-name-words",
   "comment": "Tang Clan support cut-in (SkillCut_Brother1, cloned into /[UI]/MainUI/Level_2/CutInPanels; it plays only for the brother1 skill, the one BattleSkillController with _cutIn=1). Name/Char (1..6) are six 250x250 boxes, anchored and pivoted at their centre, holding one calligraphic glyph each (唐 門 暗 器 總 綱, LeanLocalizedText keys BattleSkill/Brother1/Skill_1_1..6, DFT_S5 180 -> Palatino 162, Wrap/Truncate). In English each box gets a word - Tang (XUnity), Clan / Hidden / Weapon / General / Principles (LOM_Strings_EN); with the strings plugin off XUnity gives Tang / Gate / Darkness. / Vessel / Total / Reign - 336-713px wide at 162, so UGUI breaks every word and Truncate keeps only its first line: 'Ta' 'Cla' 'Hi' 'We' 'Ge' 'Pri'. The Name Animator (Brother1_Skill1_Intro, 1 s) writes every Char's anchoredPosition, localScale, rotation and colour each frame (glyphs fly in 1/6 s apart in 1..6 order and land on their serialized spots), so no rule can move them; sizeDelta and alignment are not animated. skillcut-name-word-1..6 size each box so its UpperLeft corner lands on a flush-left stack at x=60, 80px pitch from y=40: the words read top to bottom in key order at 64px (Principles 282px; a 64px Palatino word is ~64px of ink from ascender to descender, under the 80px pitch), on the dark field left of the art, and still arrive one by one - the fly-in scale and rotation now pivot on the far-off box centre, so each word swings in along an arc instead of spinning in place. onTextChange re-asserts 64 after FontMap's one-off 0.9 rescale and after Lean/XUnity set the text.",
   "paths": [
    "**/SkillCut*/Name/Char (*)"
   ],
   "text": {
    "bestFit": false,
    "fontSize": 64,
    "hOverflow": "Overflow",
    "vOverflow": "Overflow",
    "alignment": "UpperLeft"
   },
   "onTextChange": true
