  {
   "id": "skillcut-dialog-line",
   "comment": "Speech line on the Tang Clan cut-in: SkillDialogPanel (on Dialog/Content, _dialogs2 = BattleSkill/Brother1/Dialog_1_1) instantiates SkillDialogText - a 0x20 box, 24px, horizontal Wrap, vertical Overflow, lineSpacing 0.7 - into Dialog/Content (HorizontalLayoutGroup, no size control) and types the line into it. A 0-wide Wrap box is the vertical-Chinese trick: 'Who dares to touch my Junior Brother!' becomes 31 one-letter lines (34px + 30 x 24.1px = ~760px) from y=525, past the 168x420 scroll (ends y=930) and ~200px below the bottom of the screen. 150px wide (the group centres it, 9px in from each scroll edge) and lineSpacing 1.0, since at 0.7 the lines are 24.1px apart for ~27px of Latin ink: 4 lines ('Who dares / to touch my / Junior / Brother!') = 138px.",
   "paths": [
    "**/SkillCut*/Dialog/Content/SkillDialogText(Clone)"
   ],
   "rect": {
    "width": 150
   },
   "text": {
    "lineSpacing": 1.0,
